 },
 "notes": "Puts the cell at 5 <= chi(T^5) <= 6 (bounds/qubit_T-m5-upper-6.json, Lean tier) and by projection chi(T^6) >= 5. The argument (docs/notes/t5_rank4_exclusion.md) depends on: (1) Fact 1, every term full along every qubit: chi(T^4) = 3, so a one-qubit slice with three visible terms is the unique rank-3 decomposition of |T>^4 (qubit_T_m4_rank3.json, completeness up to symmetry assumed as in qubit_T-m5-lower-4.json) with a local fourth term, and the residual tables of research/constructions/two_qubit_slice.py for it have no exact and no stabilizer combination at the slice ratio tau^{+-1}, tau = e^{i pi/4} tan(beta) (recomputed, results/tables.json). (2) Fact 2, at most one absent term at a two-qubit point: chi(T^3) = 3, bounds/qubit_T-m3-lower-3.json. (3) The flat lemma (every term a plane or a diagonal line, at most one line per diagonal) and the base point: all four terms visible at 00 or 01; one line on each diagonal is excluded by the same tables for the 8 rank-3 decompositions of |T>^3 at tau^{+-2} (0 exact combinations). (4) The slice structure lemma; the matcher assumes nothing beyond the base point. (5) The census covers4.json (CoverEnumerator.covers(4) at orbit qubit_T plus the 12 multisets T + (x,), x in T, over the 4 full 3-covers; span(T) holds no further state, so no dependent 4-set and no cancel-at-base multiset exists), equal up to symmetry to the full covers among the numeric enumerator's 5,205 rank-4 tuples (4,697 in 2,372 orbits) and re-enumerated by the certificate. (6) Exactness: amplitudes in Q(zeta_24), both primes 1 mod 24, modular supersets, every candidate and hit re-decided mod 2013265921 and in floating point; an undecidable block or residual raises and fails the batch (none did). (7) Controls (results/control_*.json): the rank-6 witness from its all-visible pair bases (kernel and reference), planted four-term instances of five kinds, the rank-3 decomposition of |T>^4 along a qubit pair, the census against the numeric enumerator."
}
